('693bb638-d267-4eae-a65d-d6321c31e5f0', 'Drag Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Drag Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '91391201', '91391201-Resistance-Band-Drag-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Drag Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Drag Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('693ca67d-2da3-4e87-ae43-bebe232ee6d1', 'Single Leg Heel Touch Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '70941201', '70941201-Single-Leg-Heel-Touch-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Single Leg Heel Touch Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6940f06d-5d87-4b37-b856-c6d7b4bfc308', 'Standing Balance Diagonal Cross Leg Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Balance Diagonal Cross Leg Lift is a compound movement exercise that engages your entire body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '81171201', '81171201-Standing-Balance-Diagonal-Cross-Leg-Lift-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Balance Diagonal Cross Leg Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Standing Balance Diagonal Cross Leg Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6947bc3f-af40-41a0-9614-317436f1c218', 'High Plank Knee Drop', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '71231201', '71231201-High-Plank-Knee-Drop-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Beneficial for overall core development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'High Plank Knee Drop', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('695033eb-811b-4174-8346-3e3df174f4da', 'Hip Abduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Hip Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '5971201', '05971201-Lever-Seated-Hip-Abduction_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Hip Abduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lever Seated Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6959587c-e7ca-42a8-8ea8-3c60068e01ae', 'Standing Double Prayer Push', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '94281201', '94281201-Standing-Double-Prayer-Push-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Double Prayer Push. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Double Prayer Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('695eedcb-d77b-4874-9b73-f9f46143334e', 'Lying Floor Chest Press (Resistance Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '91481201', '91481201-Resistance-Band-Lying-Floor-Chest-Press-(female)_C.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Lying Floor Chest Press. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Resistance Band Lying Floor Chest Press. 3. Lie down in the appropriate position for Resistance Band Lying Floor Chest Press. 4. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 5. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lying Floor Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6964959c-b71d-44b5-9280-033073896887', '45 Degrees Step Out', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '64341201', '64341201-45-degrees-Step-Out-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for 45 Degrees Step Out. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', '45 Degrees Step Out', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('696d2afa-6fc5-4529-a3ff-72cf5f3cb9b2', 'Single Arm Row Rack Support (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '12361201', '12361201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Row-(rack-support)_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 69, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Single Arm Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('697a0ff9-4c97-4e44-8914-9f7aa23f6c89', 'Rotary Throw (Medicine Ball)', 'Back', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this rowing movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '75341201', '75341201-Medicine-Ball-Rotary-Throw-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Rotary Throw. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Medicine Ball Rotary Throw', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('69811d17-62a0-4252-b435-f9db333c04d4', 'Lying Crossed Legs Pelvic Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this twisting movement focusing on your obliques. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '79391201', '79391201-Lying-Crossed-Legs-Pelvic-Twist-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crossed Legs Pelvic Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Crossed Legs Pelvic Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Lying Crossed Legs Pelvic Twist', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6989ce79-2280-4b0d-9cf3-3e4105487b2e', 'Unilateral Row (Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '13131201', '13131201-Lever-Unilateral-Row_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Unilateral Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'back_exercise', 'Lever Unilateral Row', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('698f32f4-b981-4cc7-b657-92329962527d', 'Downward Facing Dog', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Downward Facing Dog helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '52511201', '52511201-Downward-Facing-Dog-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Downward Facing Dog. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Downward Facing Dog', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6996eb27-016c-4912-9b16-60247a9c89bd', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Legs', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '49371201', '49371201-45-Degree-Hip-Extension-Glute-Focused-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused. 2. Set up in the starting position for 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('699732e9-ac91-48f0-9a58-a4ae306f2bf3', 'Seated Lotus Pose Hip Horizontal Rotation', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your hips with this rotation stretch that helps restore range of motion. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '54901201', '54901201-Sitting-Lotus-Pose-Hip-Horizontal-Rotation-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Lotus Pose Hip Horizontal Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Seated Lotus Pose Hip Horizontal Rotation', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('699844ac-6971-4e29-8bbb-abb51bf83292', 'Wide To Small Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Wide To Small Step is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '84051201', '84051201-Wide-to-Small-Step-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Wide To Small Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Wide To Small Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('699abd6b-2bd1-4472-8f32-dccc082e74dc', 'Lying Single Leg Curl (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '98041201', '98041201-Cable-Lying-Single-Leg-Curl-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Single Leg Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Single Leg Curl. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lying Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('69ac9937-797a-4603-9f31-5d50d2cb499f', 'Shoulder Press (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '30731201', '30731201-Dumbbell-Alternate-Shoulder-Press-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternate Shoulder Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Shoulder Press - Alternating', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('69b11e3f-da0f-48eb-bcb2-cc372664381f', 'Split Squat (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '74401201', '74401201-Split-Squat-against-Wall-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat Against Wall', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('69b3d8d3-e76b-4017-b30b-85fe8d877f0e', 'Standing Cross Over High Reverse Fly (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Cross Over High Reverse Fly is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic flying movements. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '2251201', '02251201-Cable-Standing-Cross-over-High-Reverse-Fly_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Standing Cross Over High Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('69c27d49-937f-4bd9-8e47-10403f3aaff0', 'Squat (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '71971201', '71971201-Resistance-Band-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('69c71afc-2c5a-409e-b76d-fb2a4c0db7d1', 'Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift Hold', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '77851201', '77851201-Lying-Anterior-Pelvic-Shift-Hold-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift Hold. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift Hold. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Anterior Pelvic Shift Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('69c91e6f-25c6-4c15-86e2-439d7c1914d8', 'Side Plank Pull', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Plank Pull is a core pulling exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '60931201', '60931201-Side-Plank-Pull-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Pull', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('69cb6ffc-d19e-4ab2-acb1-48637494df58', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Barbell Wide Grip Upright Row (front Pov), an effective shoulder rowing exercise. You''ll also feel your traps working to support the movement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '70241201', '70241201-Barbell-Wide-Grip-Upright-Row-(front-POV)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Wide Grip Upright Row. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 4. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('69d20a5c-b430-4d11-b633-094199735805', 'Pronate Grip Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '39411201', '39411201-Dumbbell-Pronate-grip-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Pronate Grip Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Pronate Grip Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('69d9df82-d6c2-4290-b665-f057e8d32ed4', 'Prone Shoulders Cars', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your shoulders with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82641201', '82641201-Prone-Shoulders-CARs-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone Shoulders Cars. 2. Move into the stretch position for Prone Shoulders Cars. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Prone Shoulders Cars', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('69dc2b8a-52e1-486d-b9a1-013a6782b14b', 'Reverse Dip', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this dipping exercise for bigger arms. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '6721201', '06721201-Reverse-Dip_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Reverse Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a0b9722-6ed9-4d97-ad5e-a37ca6a6208a', 'Seated Eversion Foot (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Seated Eversion Foot isolates your calf muscles through a movement motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '86111201', '86111201-Resistance-Band-Seated-Eversion-Foot-(male)_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Eversion Foot. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Eversion Foot', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6a271d8a-1603-4b7f-8cf4-41104dc2bb47', 'Incline Fly (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '79971201', '79971201-Dumbbell-Incline-Alternate-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Alternate Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly - Alternating', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6a2aa69d-f309-4e7a-b96f-54632ce48dff', 'Half Kneeling Pallof Press (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '41931201', '41931201-Cable-Half-Kneeling-Pallof-Press_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Half Kneeling Pallof Press. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Execute the pressing motion for Cable Half Kneeling Pallof Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pallof_press', 'Half Kneeling Pallof Press', 'woodchop, plank, dead_bug', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6a2bac3d-5b6a-4e59-a7c3-5c91f4ec4dd1', 'Front To Under Knee Clap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '83911201', '83911201-Front-to-Under-Knee-Clap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Front To Under Knee Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Front To Under Knee Clap', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a31a692-6491-468c-92f6-8dbf95215c13', 'Clean And Jerk (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Glutes","Traps"}'::text[], 'This full-body movement exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Your quads, glutes, traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '45421201', '45421201-Kettlebell-Clean-and-Jerk_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Clean And Jerk. 2. Explosively pull the weight upward from the starting position. 3. Pull yourself under the weight and catch it at shoulder level. 4. Stand to complete the lift, then lower with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'clean', 'Clean And Jerk', 'clean, jerk, thruster', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('6a3bcdda-4f6e-4d88-a8ea-372caac933f6', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Kettlebell Seated Shoulder Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '68341201', '68341201-Kettlebell-Seated-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('6a490f5b-6592-4c01-99d3-8027603d4600', 'Kneeling Shoulder Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Shoulder Tap is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '46611201', '46611201-Kneeling-Shoulder-Tap-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Shoulder Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Kneeling Shoulder Tap', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a4cd46e-3b4c-44a1-b7e6-1cb85408fb76', 'Front Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Cable Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '1621201', '01621201-Cable-Front-Raise_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6a51a636-6e75-4b00-a09f-98e261cecc93', 'Dead Bug', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dead Bug is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2761201', '02761201-Dead-Bug_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Dead Bug. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dead_bug', 'Dead Bug', 'plank, bird_dog, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a588204-aa77-4bc5-b429-de20510b66d0', 'Contralateral Glute Dominant Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this movement movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75981201', '75981201-Dumbell-Contralateral-Glute-Dominant-Bulgarian-Spl.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbell Contralateral Glute Dominant Bulgarian Spl. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbell Contralateral Glute Dominant Bulgarian Spl. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Dumbell Contralateral Glute Dominant Bulgarian Spl', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6a5e2d26-3519-4dbb-8a96-5d8ce206a50f', 'Weighted Chin Up - Neutral Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this movement movement. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '81641201', '81641201-Weighted-Neutral-Grip-Chin-Up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 2. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 3. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Weighted Chin Up - Neutral Grip', 'Weighted Chin Up - Neutral Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a7827b7-448a-42f5-9934-ea4a49d576a4', 'Twisting Knee Up', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '55971201', '55971201-Twisting-Knee-Up-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twisting Knee Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twisting Knee Up', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a7c4bcf-ea4a-4234-9cdc-7930208b9678', 'Side Lying Heel And Knee Taps', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your full body. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65871201', '65871201-Side-Lying-Heel-and-Knee-Taps-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Heel And Knee Taps. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Lying Heel And Knee Taps', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a7f390e-5209-4921-8920-d7368fb36dca', 'Seated Abduction Twist (Chair) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Seated Alternate Abduction Twist On A Chair. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '82021201', '82021201-Sitting-Alternate-Abduction-Twist-on-a-Chair-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Alternate Abduction Twist On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Seated Abduction Twist On A Chair - Alternating', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a82a4e8-4de2-497c-ac1e-2cc96996a6a4', 'Seated Forward Roll Up (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '84341201', '84341201-Seated-Forward-Roll-Up-on-a-Chair-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Seated Forward Roll Up On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a856b7d-a518-44bc-8596-a4519671c7b1', 'Suitcase Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Suitcase Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '105441201', '105441201-Suitcase-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Suitcase Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a8851ba-de7c-40da-81b6-0fa803d2c4e5', 'Standing Rear Delt Row - Rope Attachment (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise works your rear delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '28821201', '28821201-Cable-Standing-Rear-Delt-Row-(with-rope)-(female)_shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Rear Delt Row. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Standing Rear Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6a8a11e2-1d20-4c1b-96a3-fdcea85a82c9', 'Twist Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '8211201', '08211201-Twist-Sit-up_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Sit Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Twist Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a953cf5-f03a-4284-b1a8-61683b14d807', 'Split Stance Torso Twist (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Medicine Ball Split Stance Torso Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '105521201', '105521201-Medicine-Ball-Split-Stance-Torso-Twist-(male)_Wai.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Split Stance Torso Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Medicine Ball Split Stance Torso Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Medicine Ball Split Stance Torso Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6a9ef760-9c52-45f8-858b-2740afe0c76f', 'Straight Leg Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '1161201', '01161201-Barbell-Straight-Leg-Deadlift_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Straight Leg Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6aa6248c-12fd-4845-b68b-41cde7c269cc', 'Squat (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Cable Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94231201', '94231201-Cable-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6aa9669e-859d-4de7-ae8f-7b60505fb779', 'Roll Tibialis Anterior (single Leg) Lying On Floor', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Roll Tibialis Anterior (single Leg) Lying On Floor is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54371201', '54371201-Roll-Tibialis-Anterior-(Single-Leg)-Lying-on-Floor.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Tibialis AnteriorLying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Tibialis AnteriorLying On Floor. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'foam_roll', 'Roll Tibialis Anterior Lying On Floor', 'Roll Tibialis Anterior Lying On Floor', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6aaaa117-e112-4a54-bae6-2f2914bcace5', 'Run And Semi Squat Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '32721201', '32721201-Run-and-Semi-Squat-Jump-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 4. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. This exercise is excellent for cardio development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Run And Semi Squat Jump', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ab65a70-e837-4c81-83b2-5e4a81b86d8a', 'Incline Press - Reverse Grip (Smith Machine)', 'Arms', 'Smith Machine', '{"Upper Chest","Triceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Smith Incline Reverse Grip Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '7581201', '07581201-Smith-Incline-Reverse-Grip-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Incline Reverse Grip Press. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Smith Incline Press - Reverse Grip', 'Incline Press - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6abb117d-e431-4ee2-8a40-1917ffe66e4e', 'Standing Single Arm Cross Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this raising exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '54581201', '54581201-Dumbbell-Standing-Single-Arm-Cross-Raise_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Standing Single Arm Cross Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 79, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Single Arm Cross Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6ac668bd-7db0-437e-8e20-f39c971bec26', 'Sphynx Cat Cow Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Sphynx Cat Cow Stretch provides a deep stretch for your spine, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your core provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '81681201', '81681201-Sphynx-Cat-Cow-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Sphynx Cat Cow Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Sphynx Cat Cow Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ac6b564-092f-4e06-b234-340b32836bbe', 'Half Plyo Squat Core Shift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Half Plyo Squat Core Shift is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '78451201', '78451201-Half-Plyo-Squat-Core-Shift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. An effective movement for your legs routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Half Plyo Squat Core Shift', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6addb3dc-252f-40aa-8469-8fda72638af3', 'Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '68001201', '68001201-Dumbbell-Military-Press-Russian-Twist-with-Legs-Floor-Off_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off, extending through the target muscles. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6ae3b613-5710-4447-957e-db48fc641cfa', 'Narrow Leg Bench Bridge', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Narrow Leg Bench Bridge is a core rowing exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6321201', '06321201-Narrow-Leg-Bench-Bridge-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Great for building strength in your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Narrow Leg Bench Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6af939c7-e957-4873-8ba7-a618a226216f', 'Clean And Press (Barbell)', 'Full Body', 'Barbell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Quads","Glutes","Traps","Hamstrings","Upper Back","Core"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Clean And Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your quads, glutes, traps working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '36481201', '36481201-Barbell-Clean-and-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Clean And Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Olympic Lift, Overhead Press', 'Push, Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'clean', 'Clean And Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6af97685-b9a1-47a6-88fe-7d31d148e9b3', 'Criss Cross Arms Lift', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Criss Cross Arms Lift is a movement exercise that targets your chest muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '55701201', '55701201-Criss-Cross-Arms-Lift-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Criss Cross Arms Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Arms Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b0a38d3-9281-4edf-b172-af010034c3d6', 'Hands Up Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'The Hands Up Butt Kick is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic kicking movements. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '93821201', '93821201-Hands-Up-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hands Up Butt Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Hands Up Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b16c252-2020-4408-a7ae-657535f12fa2', 'Knee Raise Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '42871201', '42871201-Knee-Raise-Stretch-(male)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Knee Raise Stretch. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Knee Raise Stretch', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b235752-6119-407d-b722-95ea73df5760', 'Reverse Spider Curl (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'The Band Reverse Spider Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68491201', '68491201-Band-Reverse-Spider-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Reverse Spider Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Reverse Spider Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6b262b9b-7cae-466c-9270-3c4c5b301886', 'Standing Shoulder Flexion', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Shoulder Flexion is a flexion exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '101471201', '101471201-Standing-Shoulder-Flexion-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Shoulder Flexion. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Shoulder Flexion', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b2b7dca-0722-4c26-9dd3-8b1722a86522', 'Bench Dip (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dipping movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '47281201', '47281201-Dumbbell-Bench-Dip_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bench Dip. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Bench Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6b349c38-d51b-4ecb-92bc-ccdacfbae7bd', 'Incline Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Barbell Incline Bench Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '471201', '00471201-Barbell-Incline-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the chest.', 'Horizontal/Incline Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Slightly wider than shoulder length', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Bench Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6b36b8f3-9fea-4658-9fe9-b941f6d5cdc9', '45 Degrees Reverse Fly (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Cable 45 Degrees Reverse Fly is a flying exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '88781201', '88781201-Cable-45-degrees-Reverse-Fly-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable 45 Degrees Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', '45 Degrees Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6b3e847e-3cae-470f-8a98-9065b52b2495', 'Single Arm Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this curling exercise. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '69971201', '69971201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Wrist-Curl-(female)_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Single Arm Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6b45d145-eb81-4e7c-b70a-feb5a83e7fe4', 'Leg Curl (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '10831201', '10831201-Suspender-Leg-Curl-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Leg Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Suspender Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('6b461094-77d0-496a-8a9c-58aeb0b4e610', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your lateral delts with the Dumbbell One Arm Lateral Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '25911201', '25911201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6b4847cb-af09-4c1d-b9f6-ca8e5086dfd1', 'Side Bend Side Leg Lift', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '74841201', '74841201-Side-Bend-Side-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Bend Side Leg Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend Side Leg Lift', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b4fe56d-7c3a-4193-8eee-eecaf2a01a34', 'Double Heel Lift Sit (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Double Heel Lift Sit Against Wall isolates your calf muscles through a movement motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '89651201', '89651201-Double-Heel-Lift-Sit-agains-Wall-(male)_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Double Heel Lift Sit Against Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Double Heel Lift Sit Against Wall', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b50a893-a50c-4fcf-a118-7150ca30e302', 'Twist Knee Drive', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '77391201', '77391201-Twist-Knee-Drive-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Knee Drive. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Twist Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b627d05-2498-4eae-a00b-f8e0c6d2c2ff', 'High To Low Woodchopper (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '83181201', '83181201-Cable-High-to-Low-Woodchopper-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable High To Low Woodchopper. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'High To Low Woodchopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6b83e759-15ed-46c3-967b-5d2a0da717b3', 'Calf Raise (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Suspender Calf Raise isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '11541201', '11541201-Suspender-Calf-Raise-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Calf Raise. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Suspender Calf Raise', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('6b96d929-6a74-4303-ba2d-1dad2c638b59', 'Boxing Duck And Uppercut', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Boxing Duck And Uppercut builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '67301201', '67301201-Boxing-Duck-and-Uppercut-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Boxing Duck And Uppercut. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Boxing Duck And Uppercut', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6b9bcc4c-19bd-4d9b-bae8-852e801898af', 'Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '24401201', '24401201-Barbell-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Horizontal Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6bada164-b283-4f66-9f33-f3975963f9f7', 'Side Hip Abduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hip Abduction Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '27591201', '27591201-Lever-Side-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Side Hip Abduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lever Side Hip Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lever Side Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6bb6b162-980d-4df4-a3a2-043ecc85e03c', 'Pull Up - Negative (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '73851201', '73851201-Pull-up-(negative)-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6bbb533c-cf17-4dc9-94e4-26e664cf26f7', 'Horizontal Pallof Press (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Horizontal Pallof Press is a core pressing exercise that primarily targets your abs. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '80431201', '80431201-Cable-Horizontal-Pallof-Press-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Horizontal Pallof Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Cable Horizontal Pallof Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pallof_press', 'Horizontal Pallof Press', 'woodchop, plank, dead_bug', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6bc953a4-7e50-4df0-ae80-0073087e88ec', 'Long Standing Hip Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Long Lever Standing Hip Extension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '93241201', '93241201-Long-Lever-Standing-Hip-Extension-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Long Lever Standing Hip Extension. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Long Lever Standing Hip Extension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Long Lever Standing Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6bcffb3f-e9f6-40a5-a2ab-3ba6179c5bfb', 'Ardha Matsyendrasana Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Ardha Matsyendrasana Yoga Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '61211201', '61211201-Ardha-Matsyendrasana-Yoga-Pose-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Ardha Matsyendrasana Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Ardha Matsyendrasana Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('6bd045af-48cd-468c-9c0b-01db0dd566d8', 'Goblet 2 Sec Hold Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '48161201', '48161201-Dumbbell-Goblet-2-sec-Hold-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet 2 Sec Hold Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet 2 Sec Hold Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6bd74300-1035-4016-ae4c-ac145ed0e571', 'Kneeling Lat Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '42981201', '42981201-Kneeling-Lat-Stretch-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Lat Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Kneeling Lat Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6bf21f1c-d51d-423b-a6a9-4a5b4ac7b820', 'Seated Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '22361201', '22361201-Dumbbell-Seated-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Lateral Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6bf2d002-d280-4a28-b68f-0d7d86a32765', 'Side Bend Arm Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Side Bend Arm Stretch provides a deep stretch for your obliques, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your lats, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '63781201', '63781201-Side-Bend-Arm-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Side Bend Arm Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend Arm Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6c098b63-4223-43c5-9371-ba48227d85fa', 'Two Arm Triceps Kickback (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Two Arm Triceps Kickback targets your triceps through a kicking motion. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '17281201', '17281201-Cable-Two-Arm-Tricep-Kickback_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Two Arm Triceps Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Two Arm Triceps Kickback', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6c421d3a-2640-45a3-80f8-69ef26bf03fa', 'Frog Crunch Feet Together', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '62831201', '62831201-Frog-Crunch-Feet-Together-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Perfect for targeting your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Frog Crunch Feet Together', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6c47e310-e0e1-4f67-a1d2-d5ef5ee45912', 'Reverse Preacher Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3841201', '03841201-Dumbbell-Reverse-Preacher-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Reverse Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Reverse Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6c53f1fe-c5f2-44ab-8ac2-dfc9e4a40590', 'Curtsey Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '51771201', '51771201-Curtsey-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Works well for quads activation.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Curtsey Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6c58b568-ed17-44d3-8244-104484344109', 'Lying Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '1871201', '01871201-Cable-Lying-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Triceps Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Triceps Extension. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6c6247e3-bbf9-45ad-8285-ca87ac248c27', 'Step (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '55251201', '55251201-Lever-Step-(VERSION-2)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Step. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lever Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6c68d075-dc2e-4a77-b921-a2172d91f681', 'Seated Row To Neck - Rope (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise works your upper back for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '106001201', '106001201-Cable-Seated-Row-to-Neck-(rope-attachment)_Should.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Row To Neck. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Seated Row To Neck', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6c6db9e5-69a3-4eb7-8568-47715f024caa', 'Walking Front Kick Vertical Hands', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93801201', '93801201-Walking-Front-Kick-Vertical-Hands-(female)_Plyomet.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking Front Kick Vertical Hands. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Front Kick Vertical Hands', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6c9ae37f-e197-4bbc-a9f5-5080186fb037', 'Air Bike (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Air Bike', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '72121201', '72121201-Resistance-Band-Air-Bike-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Wais.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Air Bike. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Air Bike. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 40, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Air Bike', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6c9bff50-603d-4940-8f86-664ecbe5397f', 'High Pulley Straight Bar Overhead Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable High Pulley Straight Bar Overhead Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a pulling motion. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '58741201', '58741201-Cable-High-Pulley-Straight-Bar-Overhead-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'High Pulley Straight Bar Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6ca30cd1-5d0f-446b-a72b-da14e9ad7dd0', 'Bent Knee Good Morning (Smith Machine)', 'Back', 'Smith Machine', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this movement exercise. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7491201', '07491201-Smith-Bent-Knee-Good-morning_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Bent Knee Good Morning. 2. Set up in the starting position for Smith Bent Knee Good Morning. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Smith Bent Knee Good Morning', 'Bent Knee Good Morning', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6ca7bd8c-616a-4c0c-85c3-8f9db574b4dc', 'Twist - Up Down (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Band Twist (up Down). You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '9321201', '09321201-Band-twist-(up-down)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Band Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6ca9ff8a-5190-45d3-ba87-a099f5cf2758', 'Side Lying Single Arm Triceps Push Up', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Side Lying Single Arm Triceps Push Up is an arm pushing exercise targeting your chest. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '69211201', '69211201-Side-Lying-Single-Arm-Triceps-Push-up-(male)_Upper.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Side Lying Single Arm Triceps Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6cd27fd6-2976-4e69-9fcf-d53b1590102d', 'Kneeling Thoracic Rotation', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'Target your thoracic spine with this rotation stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '80521201', '80521201-Kneeling-Thoracic-Rotation-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Kneeling Thoracic Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'spinal_stretch', 'Kneeling Thoracic Rotation', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6cd5eb4e-39a4-4738-8ffb-fb0030884be9', 'Skater Arm Swing', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this swinging exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '59571201', '59571201-Skater-Arm-Swings-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. A solid choice for plyometrics day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'skater', 'Skater Arm Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6cdb7cc3-253d-4c77-bd58-f4e54da349da', 'Lying Heel Touchers - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '61201', '00061201-Alternate-Heel-Touchers_waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternate Heel Touchers. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Heel Touchers - Alternating', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6cff9af9-3c9e-4036-b331-87661514d9ef', 'Standing Single Arm Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '4231201', '04231201-Dumbbell-Standing-One-Arm-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Dumbbell Standing One Arm Extension. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 79, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Single Arm Extension', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6d22238c-a861-4065-8dd4-2a82b05f0d9d', 'Split Squat (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Smith Split Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7691201', '07691201-Smith-Split-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Smith Split Squat', 'Split Squat', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6d414cdc-b1e8-47c1-8d6d-fefcd11802de', 'Leg Over Knee Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '46701201', '46701201-Leg-Over-Knee-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. A solid choice for legs day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Leg Over Knee Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6d4a4b46-50ca-45f8-af4c-cae57f3c5c4d', 'Kneeling Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65691201', '65691201-Kneeling-Leg-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Kneeling Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6d4b2c0f-e953-4a13-9eab-de03b021237b', 'Lying Leg Curl (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '5861201', '05861201-Lever-Lying-Leg-Curl_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lying Leg Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lever Lying Leg Curl. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Lying Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6d4bfef4-3e03-42cc-bb71-94dd99b0bf1b', 'Incline Row (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '25031201', '25031201-Barbell-Incline-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Row', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Incline Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6d6aa536-4c3c-43a2-92df-5711523ecfbb', 'Lying Legs Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this curling movement focusing on your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '55751201', '55751201-Bodyweight-Lying-Legs-Curl-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Bodyweight Lying Legs Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lying Legs Curl (Bodyweight', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6d7c5956-1296-45ec-ac57-2334b147ddf3', 'Military Press (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Shoulder Press Machine', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '5871201', '05871201-Lever-Military-Press-(plate-loaded)_shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Military Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Lever Military Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6d91d341-acbb-4757-9ed2-80df9ce691fa', 'Foot Tap Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Foot Tap Side Step is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '64801201', '64801201-Foot-Tap-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Foot Tap Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Foot Tap Side Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6da4ea2b-5dd6-4c6f-bec9-6a4cbadcc46a', 'Reverse Plank March', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '76731201', '76731201-Reverse-Plank-March-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. A solid choice for core day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Reverse Plank March', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6daaf726-5cb4-45bd-b177-c11a2e6ed92b', 'Standing Core Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '73011201', '73011201-Standing-Core-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Core Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Core Twist', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6dbf5aa3-dd9b-4e30-9ca4-59635774be3d', 'Lateral Step Up (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this stepping movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '24681201', '24681201-Dumbbell-Lateral-Step-Up-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lateral Step Up. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 4. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 5. Step back down with control and repeat. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Lateral Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6de36bf8-e619-4ba4-9792-53f78f97c544', 'Goblet Squat With Calf Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted squatting exercise. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74691201', '74691201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Squat-with-Calf-Raise_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Squat With Calf Raise. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Squat With Calf Raise', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6ded4fab-53cc-4567-b296-9e9e534069c7', 'Concentration Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '2971201', '02971201-Dumbbell-Concentration-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Concentration Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Concentration Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6e0d8657-e929-40bc-a9c7-c0dba40aca2f', 'Kneeling Shoulder Tap Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '64981201', '64981201-Kneeling-Shoulder-Tap-Push-Up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Kneeling Shoulder Tap Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e0e349f-9c1b-429d-8b8c-58841aa6097c', 'Olympic (Barbell) Hammer Curl', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '70661201', '70661201-Olympic-Barbell-Hammer-Curl-(female)_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Olympic Barbell Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Olympic Hammer Curl', 'Olympic Hammer Curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6e101b23-2148-41e3-8f47-61f6675dc829', 'Curtsey Lunge (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '66061201', '66061201-Smith-Curtsey-Lunge-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Curtsey Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Smith Curtsey Lunge', 'Curtsey Lunge', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6e17e223-2e4f-43b7-af7c-ff5bea0d09b0', 'Seated Pigeon Stretch (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Pigeon Stretch On A Chair provides a deep stretch for your hips, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '91661201', '91661201-Sitting-Pigeon-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_Stretch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Pigeon Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Pigeon Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e2cb60f-0caf-40f2-b812-d8c87b849118', 'Obliques Twist High Knee And Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '59601201', '59601201-Obliques-Twist-High-Knee-and-Kick-(female)_Plyomet.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Obliques Twist High Knee And Kick. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'Obliques Twist High Knee And Kick', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e2ecc03-a222-4352-883f-3a07bb582396', 'Seated Twist (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '6941201', '06941201-Seated-Twist-(on-stability-ball)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Seated Twist. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Twist. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 44, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Twist', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e515481-8d82-442f-9648-3bf1405e613f', 'PVC Front Rack Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The PVC Front Rack Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '46031201', '46031201-PVC-Front-Rack-Stretch_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for PVC Front Rack Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'PVC Front Rack Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e65c96b-d49a-4638-a9f1-8376bada14d1', 'Triangles (advanced)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Triangles (advanced) provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '88721201', '88721201-Triangles-(advanced)-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Triangles. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Triangles', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e6e3afb-4d3c-4143-8ffc-29d676d6c799', 'Bicep Curl - Under Table', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Biceps Curl Under Table is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '82741201', '82741201-Biceps-Curl-under-Table-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl Under Table', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e6e692b-68ed-42a3-91e0-9c906a8524ee', 'Standing Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4161201', '04161201-Dumbbell-Standing-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Biceps Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6e71d447-a854-491c-b025-ee017870e7f6', 'Lying Prone T Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your rear delts. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '87171201', '87171201-Lyine-Prone-T-Raise-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Prone T Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Prone T Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e800463-79f1-481d-905f-67d0d2d84431', 'Incline Fly (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Incline Fly On Exercise Ball, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '12781201', '12781201-Dumbbell-Incline-Fly-on-Exercise-Ball_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Fly On Exercise Ball. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly On Exercise Ball', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6e83be2e-a16e-442c-8420-3940a66a2055', 'Boxing Cross Hook Cross', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '67291201', '67291201-Boxing-Cross-Hook-Cross-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Boxing Cross Hook Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Boxing Cross Hook Cross', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e88e037-f63a-4979-ae89-5fac65f332a1', 'Single Leg Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '7261201', '07261201-Single-Leg-Bridge-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6e8cefc0-67c7-475f-905c-9cb08f8b81da', 'Shoulder Press (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Shoulder Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '70621201', '70621201-Cable-Shoulder-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Shoulder Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. This exercise is excellent for delts development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6ea5a26e-1114-4b74-8442-2b8d5f1c98be', 'Bent Over Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Bent Over Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '87901201', '87901201-Bodyweight-Bent-Over-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bent_over_row', 'Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ea5f614-d8cb-451f-a13f-432dcad815bc', 'Knees In And Out (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Knees In And Out On A Chair is a lower body movement exercise that targets your adductors. The hip abductors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '76621201', '76621201-Knees-In-and-Out-on-a-Chair-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up in the starting position for Knees In And Out On A Chair. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Knees In And Out On A Chair', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ebbd180-dfdb-407c-b44e-302a344117e6', 'Seated Hip Abduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hip Abduction Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '25531201', '25531201-Lever-Seated-Hip-Abduction-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Hip Abduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lever Seated Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6ec13a79-6719-4bd1-9652-f26e0eb7a9b8', 'Leg Pull', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Leg Pull provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '28491201', '28491201-Leg-Pull_Pilates_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Leg Pull. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Leg Pull', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ed4b0fc-4749-445c-acca-5c92c89c26c3', 'Incline Triceps Extension (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Incline Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '83251201', '83251201-Resistance-Band-Incline-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Ar.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Incline Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Incline Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6ed92b9a-a056-4abe-87bc-cba6d7be9479', 'Standing Shoulder Internal Rotation (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rotation movement focusing on your rotator cuff. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '91951201', '91951201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Shoulder-Internal-Rotatio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Shoulder Internal Rotation. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Resistance Band Standing Shoulder Internal Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Shoulder Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6edb00b2-5d16-4956-926c-9d89eba64867', 'Jump Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Jump Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '23741201', '23741201-Jump-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 4. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Jump Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ee66f3c-01ca-4ad5-8b5d-55bb91edc983', 'Pigeon Delt Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Pigeon Delt Raise provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '95531201', '95531201-Pigeon-Delt-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Pigeon Delt Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Move into the stretch position for Pigeon Delt Raise. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Pigeon Delt Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6eef47d5-af3f-4949-9675-ccf3a3abf458', 'Supported Single Leg Hamstrings Concentration (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this movement exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '78111201', '78111201-Cable-Supported-Single-Leg-Hamstrings-Concentratio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Supported Single Leg Hamstrings Concentration. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Supported Single Leg Hamstrings Concentration', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6ef0907b-3824-430c-888e-8fc31307f542', 'Low Row (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever Low Row (plate Loaded) is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '42141201', '42141201-Lever-Low-Row-(plate-loaded)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Low Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'cable_row', 'Lever Low Row', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6f0f6595-4d9a-48aa-8636-867dbbffafed', 'Lying Single Arm Deltoid Rear (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Dumbbell Lying One Arm Deltoid Rear, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3411201', '03411201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Deltoid-Rear_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Deltoid Rear. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Lying Single Arm Deltoid Rear', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6f10d7c4-030d-4f7e-9824-3cb38b169c23', 'Assisted Single Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '10271201', '10271201-Assisted-Single-Leg-Press_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 2. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Assisted Single Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6f204c06-fd9f-4051-9be5-154913b9285f', 'Diagonal Leg Lift Rollout (Barbell)', 'Core', 'Barbell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '103741201', '103741201-Barbell-Diagonal-Leg-Lift-Rollout_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Diagonal Leg Lift Rollout. 2. Set up in the starting position for Barbell Diagonal Leg Lift Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Diagonal Leg Lift Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6f32b1bb-ae9e-408a-a442-f9ae477af26e', 'Self Assisted Inverted Pullover', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Self Assisted Inverted Pullover is a pulling exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Your lats, triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '71001201', '71001201-Self-Assisted-Inverted-Pullover-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 2. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Self Assisted Inverted Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6f3c5a3a-4667-4c92-b852-3a8d1874fab7', 'Overhead Shoulder Press (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '83641201', '83641201-Resistance-Band-Overhead-Shoulder-Press-(VERSION-2.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Overhead Shoulder Press (. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Overhead Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6f4645f6-963a-40b5-a2b1-58174c91ac58', 'Lying Raised Shoulders Windshield Wiper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Raised Shoulders Windshield Wiper is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '78091201', '78091201-Lying-Raised-Shoulders-Windshield-Wiper-(female)_W.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Raised Shoulders Windshield Wiper. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Raised Shoulders Windshield Wiper. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Lying Raised Shoulders Windshield Wiper', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6f5d3e83-0d62-4ced-9693-9907f85f46ea', 'Decline Shrug (Kettlebell)', 'Back', 'Kettlebell, Decline Bench', '{"Traps","Upper Back"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '68161201', '68161201-Kettlebell-Decline-Shrug_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Decline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Shrug', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Decline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('6f608a73-8e12-4005-8b78-3fbc8d49c968', 'Bridge Walk Leg Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this raising movement focused on hip extension. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65351201', '65351201-Bridge-Walk-Leg-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability. Works well for glutes activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Bridge Walk Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6f70519b-290f-4982-8080-3c878422c43a', 'Standing Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '22331201', '22331201-Dumbbell-Front-Raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6f728487-d40a-4ef9-8bd9-6da5a88370c8', 'Self Ankle Mobilization', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your ankles, the Self Ankle Mobilization helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82621201', '82621201-Self-Ankle-Mobilization-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Self Ankle Mobilization. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 38, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'mobility', 'Self Ankle Mobilization', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6f7311b6-b74e-400a-b064-102709cb9dfb', 'Standing External Rotation (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This rotation exercise works your rotator cuff for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '80941201', '80941201-Resistance-Band-Standing-External-Rotation-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing External Rotation. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Resistance Band Standing External Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6f8aa377-bb7a-455f-b351-ad5d56221325', 'Assisted Wheel Rollout (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band, Ab Wheel', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Band Assisted Wheel Rollout, focusing on your abs. The lats, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '26491201', '26491201-Band-Assisted-Wheel-Rollout-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Assisted Wheel Rollout. 2. Set up in the starting position for Band Assisted Wheel Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Assisted Wheel Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('6f90f80c-2ec2-4b77-8039-af686db356e5', 'Bench Lateral Step Up (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stepping movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '67971201', '67971201-Barbell-Bench-Lateral-Step-up-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 4. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 5. Step back down with control and repeat. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Bench Lateral Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('6f9493ab-246f-471d-9c42-824f6d3db05b', 'Ring Archer Dip (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dipping exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '75211201', '75211201-Ring-Archer-Dip-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Ring Archer Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('6f9bdc47-1cd8-46b9-8ade-1d1cb43e542b', 'Wide Forward Fold Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your hamstrings with this twisting stretch that helps restore range of motion. The lower back, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '89691201', '89691201-Wide-Forward-Fold-Twist-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Wide Forward Fold Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Wide Forward Fold Twist. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Wide Forward Fold Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6f9e36f1-a596-4086-89df-2270d12f71d9', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated In Out Leg Raise With Chair, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '71371201', '71371201-Sitting-In-Out-Leg-Raise-with-Chair_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise With Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fa1d5d9-484a-4c8b-9c3a-d8a0addb43c0', 'Side Bend Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stabilization movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '65041201', '65041201-Side-Bend-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Perfect for targeting your obliques.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend Plank', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fa67d86-dd94-4679-9ecd-3af67ce2e635', 'Decline Push Up (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '71831201', '71831201-Decline-Push-up-with-Chair-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Push Up', 'Push', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Decline Push Up With Chair', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fb361a5-dd28-456d-9240-cbe1d752be72', 'Bench Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '98591201', '98591201-Lever-Bench-Leg-Press-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Bench Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Bench Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6fb87a8a-0b84-48a3-9ba4-8deb75ec0c88', 'Hip Flexor Stretch (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Hip Flexor Stretch With Chair provides a deep stretch for your hip flexors, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '73091201', '73091201-Hip-Flexor-Stretch-with-Chair-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Move into the stretch position for Hip Flexor Stretch With Chair. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Hip Flexor Stretch With Chair', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fbc05cc-5c21-4c33-b477-5ceebd5afd6c', 'Arm Slingers Hanging Straight Legs (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Arm Slingers Hanging Straight Legs is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors, grip working to support the movement. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '23331201', '23331201-Arm-slingers-Hanging-Straight-Legs_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Set up in the starting position for Arm Slingers Hanging Straight Legs. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Arm Slingers Hanging Straight Legs', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fbdad51-de44-476c-b216-95e7846c5763', '45 Degrees Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell 45 Degrees Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '98131201', '98131201-Dumbbell-45-degrees-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell 45 Degrees Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '45 Degrees Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6fcaae74-197c-4ee7-b486-4857c9f6f971', 'Deadlift (Machine)', 'Back', 'Lever Machine', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Deadlift (plate Loaded) is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '5781201', '05781201-Lever-Deadlift-(plate-loaded)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Lever Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6fcf0fbd-7a21-4afa-aa37-cfc653bff7e9', 'Standing Scapular External Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rotation movement focusing on your rotator cuff. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '93611201', '93611201-Bodyweight-Standing-Scapular-External-Rotation-(mal.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Bodyweight Standing Scapular External Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Scapular External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fdb54f5-a163-4cb0-a0a9-84cc772efb54', 'Kneeling Plank Shoulder Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '103911201', '103911201-Kneeling-Plank-Shoulder-Tap_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Kneeling Plank Shoulder Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6fe417b6-dbaf-4ac5-82bf-8e84d71d4ca0', 'Decline Bench Press (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Decline Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Smith Decline Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '74221201', '74221201-Smith-Decline-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Decline Bench Press. 2. Set the bench to a decline angle and secure your feet. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 96, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'decline_press', 'Smith Decline Bench Press', 'Decline Bench Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6fed0410-3e13-492e-a0f8-126da74eb31f', 'Standing Overhead Press (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '4141201', '04141201-Dumbbell-Standing-Alternate-Overhead-Press_Shoulde.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Alternate Overhead Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 99, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Standing Overhead Press - Alternating', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('6ff4cab5-aa9f-4e2f-b03b-f1b70cea4c7f', 'Airbike (Air Bike)', 'Core', 'Air Bike', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Air Bike is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '23951201', '23951201-Air-Bike-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Air Bike. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, 'Push/Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, 'Lying', NULL, 'Neutral', 'Standard', 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Airbike', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6ff818da-c5ed-4ea8-a5eb-1eb4b1cc05f2', 'Seated Single Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this pressing exercise for quad development. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '71071201', '71071201-Lever-Seated-Single-Leg-Press-(VERSION-2)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Leg Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 4. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Seated Single Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6ff97f60-aa25-463e-a269-88db37232eb7', 'Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '22541201', '22541201-Dumbbell-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('70061334-4a95-4d4b-b973-d2e4373bdc24', 'Heels Squat Slide (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '89561201', '89561201-Heels-Squat-Slide-Wall-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Heels Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('700aece3-e5f3-4104-9cd4-5c372a7b07a1', 'Bicep Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '91331201', '91331201-Resistance-Band-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('700c64c0-a19f-4478-84fc-12a485228763', 'Rotation Shoulder Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rotation movement focusing on your delts. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '19821201', '19821201-Rotation-Shoulder-Stretch-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Rotation Shoulder Stretch. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Rotation Shoulder Stretch', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('700d0fd8-4590-4c4d-8973-2f6e288c1087', 'Half Kneeling Shoulders Press (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Barbell Half Kneeling Shoulders Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '96941201', '96941201-Barbell-Half-Kneeling-Shoulders-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Half Kneeling Shoulders Press. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Half Kneeling Shoulders Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('700d1ec5-d9a8-4c99-9c80-722be13aa171', 'High Knee Double Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'The High Knee Double Twist is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic twisting movements. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '59351201', '59351201-High-Knee-Double-Twist-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for High Knee Double Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Double Twist', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('700d272d-bc35-4a31-ad1a-0205b7ec84dd', 'Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '43001201', '43001201-Quadriceps-stretch-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Quadriceps Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('700db7b2-b26e-4f54-819e-e1425e1d7391', 'Front Leg Elevated Split Squat (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine, Step Platform', '{Quadriceps}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Smith Front Leg Elevated Split Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '90411201', '90411201-Smith-Front-Leg-Elevated-Split-Squat-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Front Leg Elevated Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Smith Front Leg Elevated Split Squat', 'Front Leg Elevated Split Squat', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('70114775-87ed-480b-bbe8-6bc7dfa6242b', 'Runners Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '43031201', '43031201-Runners-Stretch-(female)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Runners Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Runners Stretch', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7015437e-ef1b-4e49-ba9e-e538aa20a4b5', 'Leg V Up - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '104521201', '104521201-Alternating-Leg-V-Up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternating Leg V Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'Leg V Up - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70327821-490b-4a81-af90-98df5b1eca71', 'Decline Push Up - Weighted Vest (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX, Weighted Vest', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '95071201', '95071201-Suspender-Weighted-Vest-Decline-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Weighted Vest Decline Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Push Up', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Weighted Vest Decline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('704f8bd0-bca6-4584-bdc2-f6cd25367657', 'Standing Half Bend', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '59031201', '59031201-Standing-Half-Bend-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Half Bend. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Half Bend', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('70509a1c-5c00-44ca-a5ab-64c5d3fb752b', 'Lying High Criss Cross Legs', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying High Criss Cross Legs is a lower body movement exercise that targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '78301201', '78301201-Lying-High-Criss-Cross-Legs-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying High Criss Cross Legs. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying High Criss Cross Legs. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Lying High Criss Cross Legs', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70622246-8a82-40c6-9b60-26739f254e46', 'Renegade Row - Underhand (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Dumbbell Underhand Renegade Row, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '82221201', '82221201-Dumbbell-Underhand-Renegade-Row-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Underhand Renegade Row. 2. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Underhand Renegade Row', 'Renegade Row - Underhand', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('70793e77-3a0a-4b2e-a7fc-e732d3c2911a', 'Lying Raised Heel Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Raised Heel Tap is a lower body raising exercise that targets your full body. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94401201', '94401201-Lying-Raised-Heel-Tap-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Raised Heel Tap. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Raised Heel Tap. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Raised Heel Tap', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70a2f399-6503-490b-9055-1cd4fcb8401a', 'Lying Rotator Cuff Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this rotation movement targeting your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '90361201', '90361201-Lying-Rotator-Cuff-Rotation-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Rotator Cuff Rotation. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Rotator Cuff Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Lying Rotator Cuff Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70aaac20-f7ca-4980-b228-a0b501b58a20', 'Incline Pullover (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your lats, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '83321201', '83321201-Kettlebell-Incline-Pullover-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Incline Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 61, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Incline Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('70acbd18-dce3-475c-818b-4e05d0b6f21d', 'Walking Incline (Treadmill)', 'Legs', 'Treadmill', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '52091201', '52091201-Walking-on-Incline-Treadmill-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Incline Treadmill. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 53, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'treadmill', 'Walking On Incline Treadmill', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70b393a9-6fda-48a9-a1f2-abd764a53208', 'Kneeling Rollout (EZ Bar)', 'Core', 'EZ Bar', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the EZ Bar Knelling Rollout, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '41891201', '41891201-EZ-Bar-Knelling-Rollout_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Set up in the starting position for EZ Bar Knelling Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'EZ Bar Knelling Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('70b7d36c-b240-4ae7-ab49-1deb2b81a431', 'Standing Squeeze Upper Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Squeeze Upper Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '66131201', '66131201-Cable-Standing-Squeez-Upper-Chest-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Squeeze Upper Chest Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Squeeze Upper Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('70c20a02-ed62-41c6-becf-2399353e47a2', 'Bouncing Inner Thigh Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '56761201', '56761201-Bouncing-Inner-Thigh-Tap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bouncing Inner Thigh Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Bouncing Inner Thigh Tap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70c30173-36cc-4077-aaae-87b8d01c6501', 'Abductor Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stretching movement focusing on your adductors. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '9361201', '09361201-Adductor-Stretch-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Adductor Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Abductor Stretch', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70cceb2a-c42f-427a-9ed1-7537c07fec1f', 'Goblet Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Goblet Bulgarian Split Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75491201', '75491201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Bulgarian-Split-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Bulgarian Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Goblet Bulgarian Split Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('70d910f2-1305-4c61-8d6a-4a4219e01955', 'Dish Hold', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '94861201', '94861201-Dish-Hold-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Dish Hold. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Dish Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70deea71-ef92-4dba-b3e1-babd1a9285c1', 'Seated Around The World (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Dumbbell Seated Around The World, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Your chest work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '105121201', '105121201-Dumbbell-Seated-Around-the-World_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Around The World. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Seated Around The World', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('70e3d616-8e39-4a42-abf3-2403b9a6b868', 'Standing Front Raise Above Head (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Front Raise Above Head is a raising exercise that targets your front delts for shoulder development. The standing position engages your core for stability. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '101781201', '101781201-Dumbbell-Standing-Front-Raise-Above-Head-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Front Raise Above Head. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Standing Front Raise Above Head', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('70f31411-9c68-48d6-8041-23517e2c0e85', 'Triceps Press (low Bar Position)', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Press (low Bar Position) targets your triceps through a pressing motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '48041201', '48041201-Triceps-Press-(low-bar-position)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Keep your upper arms stationary and extend at the elbow. 2. Squeeze your triceps at full extension, then control the return. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Triceps Press', 'bicep_curl, tricep_pushdown, skull_crusher, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70f49917-9c8a-4325-942a-b92fcaf19780', 'Diamond Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '45391201', '45391201-Diamond-Press_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Diamond Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('70f6d3d9-6b40-425f-8b24-a5ce7c6b1743', 'Seated Overhead Triceps Extension (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Seated Overhead Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '26061201', '26061201-Barbell-Seated-Overhead-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Seated Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, 'Push', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, 'Neutral', 'Narrow', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Seated Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('710a0d16-7947-415a-8ff4-a5e52e73b46c', 'Seated Shoulder Stretch Behind The (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Seated Shoulder Stretch Behind The is a flexibility exercise that targets your shoulders, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '89861201', '89861201-Resistance-Band-Seated-Shoulder-Stretch-Behind-the.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Shoulder Stretch Behind The. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Resistance Band Seated Shoulder Stretch Behind The. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 37, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Seated Shoulder Stretch Behind The', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('710a42a6-6a6d-4ff0-aa7a-7b1ba606147e', 'Standing Behind Head Clasp And Pushdown', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '94791201', '94791201-Standing-Behind-Head-Clasp-And-Pushdown-(female)_C.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Behind Head Clasp And Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Standing Behind Head Clasp And Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('711a01bc-08ae-4d81-971d-e2f88ca356cc', 'Behind Head Push Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pushing exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '89211201', '89211201-Behind-Head-Push-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Behind Head Push Butt Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Behind Head Push Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7146144f-f324-4c94-97fd-3015000ec6fa', 'Pronated Grip Seated Scapular Retraction Shr (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Lever Machine', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your core. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54481201', '54481201-Lever-Pronated-Grip-Seated-Scapular-Retraction-Shr.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Pronated Grip Seated Scapular Retraction Shr. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use an overhand (pronated) grip with palms facing down/away. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lever Pronated Grip Seated Scapular Retraction Shr', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('714f227d-4e7f-4b0e-bb78-cde74732efe5', 'Marching in Place', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '56901201', '56901201-Marching-On-Spot-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Marching On Spot. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Marching On Spot', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('714fb9b4-f01d-4810-9a6a-9153da545335', 'Lying Pullover (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Lying Pullover On Exercise Ball, an effective pulling movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your lats, triceps working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '12841201', '12841201-Dumbbell-Lying-Pullover-on-Exercise-Ball_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Pullover On Exercise Ball. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Pullover On Exercise Ball. 3. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 4. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Lying Pullover On Exercise Ball', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('71623528-cbdb-424c-97da-8bc51d1e8fc3', 'Star Squat Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '64011201', '64011201-Star-Squat-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. This exercise is excellent for quads development. Variation: Star Squat Jack.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Star Squat Jack', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('71694738-2a15-47e5-b4eb-6c63472f0215', 'L Sit', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '14021201', '14021201-L-sit_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for L Sit. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'L Sit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('71720f59-506a-4855-a1dd-ebf6c8bf81c3', 'Cross Body Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Cross Body Hammer Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '26461201', '26461201-Dumbbell-Cross-Body-Hammer-Curl-(Version-2)-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Cross Body Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Cross Body Hammer Curl', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('7172c857-0667-49e0-83d4-34ef76b84ba5', 'Seated Hip Rotation (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this rotation movement focused on hip extension. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '91231201', '91231201-Sitting-Hip-Rotation-on-a-Chair-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Hip Rotation On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Seated Hip Rotation On A Chair', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7174ece3-3b3b-4150-893d-931ba7a425cc', 'Lying Hip Rotation', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this rotation movement focusing on your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '73041201', '73041201-Lying-Hip-Rotation-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Rotation. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Hip Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Hip Rotation', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('717e4b2c-33ad-4502-8b65-a1f93f7bffa7', 'Straight Legs Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '42931201', '42931201-Dumbbell-Straight-Legs-Deadlift_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Straight Legs Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Legs Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('718dde79-c982-4014-8eb7-f27aacf85d9a', 'Jack Burpee', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'The Jack Burpee is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '76191201', '76191201-Jack-Burpee-(male)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Jack Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('718f58f3-95bd-4224-b224-a69b1817ee94', 'Bent Leg Side Kick (kneeling)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '30351201', '30351201-Bent-Leg-Side-Kick-(kneeling)-(male)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Bent Leg Side Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Bent Leg Side Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7195d7db-4b9e-4d8e-baf3-fcab30c2751e', 'Plank On Hands', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '95281201', '95281201-Plank-on-Hands-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. Ideal for abs strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank On Hands', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('71b5f774-2361-4938-858d-592ffad94ebd', 'Straight Leg Crossed Arms Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '88611201', '88611201-Straight-Leg-Crossed-Arms-Sit-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Straight Leg Crossed Arms Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Crossed Arms Sit Up', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('71bbeaf8-056a-49a5-b851-8eb55603f880', 'Around Pullover (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Around Pullover, an effective pulling movement for upper body strength. The lats, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '107151201', '107151201-Dumbbell-Around-Pullover-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Around Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Around Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('71d338ed-10da-4167-b7ed-f603081512dd', 'Wood Chop (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this movement exercise that strengthens your obliques. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '80251201', '80251201-Kettlebell-Wood-Chop-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Wood Chop. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Wood Chop. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 58, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Wood Chop', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('71ed359b-0eea-48be-8c0a-8f5815a4686a', 'Twin Handle Parallel Grip Lat Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '8181201', '08181201-Cable-Twin-Handle-Parallel-Grip-Lat-Pulldown_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Twin Handle Parallel Grip Lat Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Twin Handle Parallel Grip Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('71fded86-2974-469b-a5c6-e4c3f39040ba', 'Side Mountain Climber', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Mountain Climber is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. The hip flexors, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '48151201', '48151201-Side-Mountain-Climber-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Side Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72133b1f-8f26-41d9-ae77-a3f2071c687b', 'Clothespin Hold', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this movement exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '100101201', '100101201-Clothespin-Hold-(female)_Hands_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Clothespin Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Clothespin Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('721852cb-b07b-490b-8aa5-e03fd6a5dd74', 'Prone Hip Cars', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '82551201', '82551201-Prone-Hip-CARs-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone Hip Cars. 2. Set up in the starting position for Prone Hip Cars. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Prone Hip Cars', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72287d30-3553-4048-9a58-7868c7d096d7', 'Shoulder Press (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Shoulder Press Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '100671201', '100671201-Lever-Shoulder-Press-(plate-loaded)-(VERSION-3)-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Shoulder Press(. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Lever Shoulder Press (', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('723223f5-b0a2-46aa-ad32-9f72f84f050b', 'Seated Side Step (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '72601201', '72601201-Sitting-Side-Step-on-Chair-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Side Step On Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('723cbade-d081-4dff-8f7f-22b52a89288f', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Smith Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Smith Machine', '{Deltoids}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '7651201', '07651201-Smith-Seated-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Smith Seated Shoulder Press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('727588de-367c-4327-b788-b07aa494c63d', 'Plank Side Kick Through', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '69791201', '69791201-Plank-Side-Kick-Through-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. An effective movement for your core routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Side Kick Through', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72855ac1-6edb-453a-8260-88cf85f464f7', 'Wall Press And Twist (Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Wall Press And Twist. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '55931201', '55931201-Wall-Press-and-Twist-(Male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Wall Press And Twist, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Wall Press And Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72898a9e-ba04-404c-ac12-b2b5712d26ef', 'Burpee', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Your chest, quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '11601201', '11601201-Burpee_Cardio-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7289e413-4f4e-45a1-86f5-4438d3765a23', 'Parsva Balasana Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Parsva Balasana Yoga Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '46101201', '46101201-Parsva-Balasana-Yoga-Pose_Stretching.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Parsva Balasana Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Parsva Balasana Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('728a2297-08b0-4873-8ac5-c30c24fec03b', 'Kneeling Dynamic Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Kneeling Dynamic Plank, focusing on your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '66471201', '66471201-Kneeling-Dynamic-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Kneeling Dynamic Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('728cd641-9ad3-4340-a869-cdc05db74a42', '4 Cone Single Foot Lateral Hops (Cones)', 'Legs', 'Cones', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '90671201', '90671201-4-Cone-Single-Foot-Lateral-Hops-(male)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for 4 Cone Single Foot Lateral Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', '4 Cone Single Foot Lateral Hops', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72945233-499c-4ffe-a6dc-3b0c03428b95', 'Kneeling Back Rotation Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Back Rotation Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your back, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78011201', '78011201-Kneeling-Back-Rotation-Stretch-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Kneeling Back Rotation Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Kneeling Back Rotation Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('729ed491-9e52-4292-a64d-882d5adb7e20', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Low Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '79841201', '79841201-Bodyweight-Standing-Straight-Arm-Chest-Low-Fly-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.60311+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72a4ca9f-52ac-4268-83f4-c8f0d1204cc3', 'Seated Side Crunch Elbow To Knee (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Side Crunch Elbow To Knee On Chair targets your obliques through a crunching motion, building rotational core strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '104981201', '104981201-Seated-Side-Crunch-Elbow-to-Knee-on-Chair-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated Side Crunch Elbow To Knee On Chair', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72a7aa94-98fd-490a-bf93-e12b9f37a1fd', 'Bench Press - Close Grip (EZ Bar)', 'Chest', 'EZ Bar, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The EZ Bar Close Grip Bench Press targets your triceps through a pressing motion. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '24331201', '24331201-EZ-bar-Close-Grip-Bench-Press-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'close_grip_bench', 'EZ Bar Bench Press - Close Grip', 'EZ Bar Bench Press - Close Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('72af334a-d9a2-4dde-a5c6-9ddd323dcc5c', 'Standing Face Pull - Rope (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Standing Face Pull (with Rope), an effective shoulder pulling exercise. Secondary activation of your upper back, rotator cuff provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '56561201', '56561201-Cable-Standing-Face-Pull-(with-rope)_Shoulders-FIX.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Face Pull. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Standing Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('72b9b12e-87ee-4ce4-9e13-8d97e680900a', 'Back Leg Lift Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '66441201', '66441201-Back-Leg-Lift-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Back Leg Lift Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Back Leg Lift Jack', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72c36aac-c18e-4e66-8426-db5557fc8d97', 'Wide Legged Forward Fold', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your hamstrings area and enhance overall flexibility. The lower back, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '97691201', '97691201-Wide-Legged-Forward-Fold-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Wide Legged Forward Fold. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Wide Legged Forward Fold', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72c651a7-53af-4cdb-8e0b-2f32a4491829', 'Triceps Dip On High Parallel Bars (Dip Bars)', 'Arms', 'Dip Bars', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Dip On High Parallel Bars is an arm dipping exercise targeting your chest. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '81431201', '81431201-Triceps-Dip-on-High-Parallel-Bars-(male)_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Triceps Dip On High Parallel Bars', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72c8082a-3065-48b8-9469-75a253d7afa6', 'Jump Rope (Jump Rope)', 'Full Body', 'Jump Rope', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Your quads, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '5111201', '05111201-Jump-Rope-(female)_Cardio-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jump Rope. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jump_rope', 'Jump Rope', 'running, jumping_jack, high_knees', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72cf26ae-4a8c-4079-85ec-a5355c0c90b3', 'Plyo Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Plyo Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '3711201', '03711201-Dumbbell-Plyo-Squat_thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plyo Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 97, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Plyo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
