('72f04225-3c68-4dd1-9d47-165f95b851b0', 'Turn Side Step 4 Corner Touches', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '57921201', '57921201-Turn-Side-Step-4-Corner-Touches-(male)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Turn Side Step 4 Corner Touches. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Turn Side Step 4 Corner Touches', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('72f5bc4e-2732-4f9a-84e2-0f849c5de7dd', 'Twist (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Cable Twist. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '2431201', '02431201-Cable-Twist_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('73006eda-08d3-4c6e-ac62-38e3d37e43ee', 'Sphinx Pose Twist', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Sphinx Pose Twist helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '87601201', '87601201-Sphinx-Pose-Twist-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Sphinx Pose Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Sphinx Pose Twist. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Sphinx Pose Twist', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7307a83b-2b53-4219-8c72-f77b1557d04c', 'Standing Split Yoga Pose Urdhva Prasarita Eka Pada', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Split Yoga Pose Urdhva Prasarita Eka Pada is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The standing position engages your core for stability. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '76061201', '76061201-Standing-Split-Yoga-Pose-Urdhva-Prasarita-Eka-Pada.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Split Yoga Pose Urdhva Prasarita Eka Pada. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Standing Split Yoga Pose Urdhva Prasarita Eka Pada', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('731440dc-2892-4b2c-b752-69a66725ad6e', 'Weighted Donkey Calf Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Weighted Donkey Calf Raise isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '8331201', '08331201-Weighted-Donkey-Calf-Raise_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 2. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 3. Lower with control and repeat. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Weighted Donkey Calf Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7344887f-8e1f-4973-bc31-c76fe1728104', 'Single Dead Bug', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '67211201', '67211201-Single-Dead-Bug-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Single Dead Bug. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dead_bug', 'Single Dead Bug', 'plank, bird_dog, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73464583-4091-4e6f-9333-ebdde925b78d', 'Decline Shrug (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Traps","Upper Back"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Decline Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '3051201', '03051201-Dumbbell-Decline-Shrug_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Shrug', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Decline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('734e31ef-8995-4421-8b14-a388ebc442ef', 'Lying Single Leg Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '28551201', '28551201-Lying-Single-Leg-Kick-(female)_Pilates_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Single Leg Kick. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Single Leg Kick. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Single Leg Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('735f4a96-1c6e-4e01-93a1-4dbc6d8c1697', 'Curtsey Lunge Knee Up', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Curtsey Lunge Knee Up is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic lunging movements. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '73491201', '73491201-Curtsey-Lunge-Knee-up-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Include this in your plyometrics training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Curtsey Lunge Knee Up', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('736427dd-158f-4861-9097-31bd4f1f514e', 'Lying Frog Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '60231201', '60231201-Lying-Frog-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Frog Kick. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Frog Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Frog Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('736d32d3-948e-4c7f-ba00-158dfee687a2', 'Standing Push And Toe Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Push And Toe Tap builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '85221201', '85221201-Standing-Push-and-Toe-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Push And Toe Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Push And Toe Tap', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7373e565-dabd-4f40-8cfa-f03c8d2b3d89', 'Hamstring Curl Double Kick (Gymnastic Rings) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity curling exercise that challenges your entire body. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '56031201', '56031201-Alternating-Hamstring-Curl-Double-Kick-(female)_Pl.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Hamstring Curl Double Kick - Alternating', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('737891df-8157-4661-a52c-e0d7b9c6c8f2', 'Bent Over Back Extension Scapular Adduction', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your erector spinae with this extension exercise for a stronger posterior chain. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '88961201', '88961201-Bent-Over-Back-Extension-Scapular-Adduction-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Bent Over Back Extension Scapular Adduction', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73851bd7-5e49-4c49-9d12-ffbf8c00e25f', 'Reverse Plank On Elbows', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '88971201', '88971201-Reverse-Plank-on-Elbows-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. This exercise is excellent for abs development. Variation: Reverse Plank On Elbows.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Reverse Plank On Elbows', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7386015b-035c-4f7b-807f-54c0aeb064fd', 'Single Arm Incline Chest Press (Plate Loaded)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Lever One Arm Incline Chest Press (plate Loaded) is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '55761201', '55761201-Lever-One-Arm-Incline-Chest-Press-(plate-loaded)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever One Arm Incline Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 76, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Lever Single Arm Incline Chest Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('738baeda-fe95-432f-90f6-70b8878e467d', 'Leg Raise Above Head And Under Knee Clap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '66411201', '66411201-Leg-Raise-Above-Head-and-Under-Knee-Clap-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Leg Raise Above Head And Under Knee Clap', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73a2bbd6-d866-43ba-9ef1-336e258c8eba', 'Cambered Bar Lying Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '52671201', '52671201-Cambered-Bar-Lying-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cambered Bar Lying Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Cambered Bar Lying Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73a71825-0aef-431f-a01b-702aaf047d66', 'Outward Calf Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105311201', '105311201-Outward-Calf-Raise-(male)_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 2. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 3. Lower with control and repeat. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Outward Calf Raise', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73b45134-9c3c-4c34-8db7-b9a3fb2b50ac', 'Wrist Full Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Wrist Full Push Up, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '69821201', '69821201-Wrist-Full-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Wrist Full Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73b77b58-d3a4-4a70-9ce2-35d327942eb3', 'Lat Shoulder Stretch Into Shoulder Shrug', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your shoulders area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '78871201', '78871201-Lat-Shoulder-Stretch-into-Shoulder-Shrug-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 2. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 3. Move into the stretch position for Lat Shoulder Stretch Into Shoulder Shrug. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Lat Shoulder Stretch Into Shoulder Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73c86fec-117a-4801-a6c3-799200590e25', 'Seated Overhead Under Knee Clap On A Ch - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Alternate Overhead Under Knee Clap On A Ch is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '82011201', '82011201-Sitting-Alternate-Overhead-Under-Knee-Clap-on-a-Ch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Overhead Under Knee Clap On A Ch - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73cf254a-35a1-43dd-9b1f-db52f39a57e2', 'Split Sprinter Low Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '70961201', '70961201-Split-Sprinter-Low-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'sprint', 'Split Sprinter Low Lunge', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73d9a494-5dcd-40c0-82a5-c051c19d5a96', 'Sled Backward Angled Calf Raise (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '64901201', '64901201-Sled-Backward-Angled-Calf-Raise_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 2. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 3. Lower with control and repeat. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Sled Backward Angled Calf Raise', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('73e5d4f1-ffac-4b91-885b-11a1df3f2089', 'Twist And Leg Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Twist And Leg Lift builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '65311201', '65311201-Twist-and-Leg-Lift-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist And Leg Lift. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist And Leg Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73f1cd4b-16ab-439a-b69a-deb536b95c60', 'Plyo Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57451201', '57451201-Plyo-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. Works well for quads activation.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Plyo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('73f4050e-30b3-4cbf-8a4f-b0a729d8dc22', 'Goblet Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Goblet Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '23561201', '23561201-Kettlebell-Goblet-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Goblet Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('73ff5952-f95f-43be-9d88-d0be89ec8d52', 'Rotary Calf (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted movement exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '31051201', '31051201-Lever-Rotary-Calf-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Rotary Calf. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lever Rotary Calf. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Rotary Calf', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('7406e76d-888c-4a29-b680-350d52776672', 'Standing Stacked Arms Lift', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '87421201', '87421201-Standing-Stacked-Arms-Lift-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Stacked Arms Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Stacked Arms Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7413e8c6-fbb9-44d1-935e-543d5bc4ad89', 'Push Up To Side Plank', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '6641201', '06641201-Push-Up-to-Side-Plank_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Push Up To Side Plank', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7420bbea-1f40-4abb-847b-33ce28a0e781', 'Pelvic Tilt Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Pelvic Tilt Hold is a lower body movement exercise that targets your abs. You''ll also feel your lower back working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '77991201', '77991201-Pelvic-Tilt-Hold-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Pelvic Tilt Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Pelvic Tilt Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7425b85c-d720-4a1d-97f8-7b8240e46870', 'Arms Forward Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '56241201', '56241201-Arms-Forward-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arms Forward Butt Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Arms Forward Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7433d205-8487-4132-b542-859728f87df0', 'Sit (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Sit (wall) is a movement exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7341201', '07341201-Sit-(wall)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Sit. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Sit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7435e4e9-e8d6-429b-a78b-480d0e5140b0', 'Rotational Push Up Knee Tap', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Rotational Push Up Knee Tap, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '74601201', '74601201-Rotational-Push-Up-Knee-Tap_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Include this in your chest training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Rotational Push Up Knee Tap', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('743697a5-a431-45a2-9bc3-bc37b7f2a26d', 'Butterfly Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this flying exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '77611201', '77611201-Butterfly-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Butterfly Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7440c75b-2fa1-424c-8651-dd0ac6e0cec0', 'Bench Press (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '66191201', '66191201-Kettlebell-Bench-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('744ce34f-1fc3-4559-beee-72d6ba4cfc33', 'Reverse Lunge Forward Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74581201', '74581201-Reverse-Lunge-Forward-Lunge-(male)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Reverse Lunge Forward Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('744e3fe3-9719-42dc-bafc-2b6f370d3eea', 'Spinal Stretch (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stretching movement that works your abs. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '7791201', '07791201-Spinal-Stretch-(on-stability-ball)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Spinal Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Spinal Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 32, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'spinal_stretch', 'Spinal Stretch', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'stability_ball', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7452eecd-ffec-43ca-9f3c-ccb2f66894f5', 'Squat Side Power Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '46381201', '46381201-Squat-Side-Power-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Side Power Kick', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7464fe7c-03cc-47e7-b3be-5caf1a35ec8f', 'Landmine Single Leg Hip Thrust (Landmine)', 'Legs', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65461201', '65461201-Landmine-Single-Leg-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Landmine Single Leg Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('74674edc-6b53-494c-a438-2812f6ac3c77', 'Side Step Downward Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side Step Downward Punch builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '84611201', '84611201-Side-Step-Downward-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Downward Punch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Side Step Downward Punch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74726802-84dc-45fc-9ff6-155e4f84dbdb', 'Standing Pec Fly (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Fly Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever Standing Pec Fly is a flying exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '93981201', '93981201-Lever-Standing-Pec-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Pec Fly. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lever Standing Pec Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('7478d41e-d042-4883-a8c3-9dfc73fbbdb8', 'Lying Single Leg Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lying Single Leg Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '72911201', '72911201-Lying-Single-Leg-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Single Leg Abduction. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lying Single Leg Abduction', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('747fb262-ee34-4d8d-8683-387ef733201e', 'Upright Row - Under Two Feet (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Band Upright Row (under Two Feet) is a rowing exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your traps working to support the movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '81051201', '81051201-Band-Upright-Row-(Under-two-feet)-(female)_Shoulde.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Upright Row. 2. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 3. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'Upright Row', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, shrug', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('74831288-79c5-4e1f-9b1d-47b7a7c082a7', 'Decline Crunch (Plate, Decline Bench)', 'Core', 'Decline Bench, Weight Plate', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Weighted Decline Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '70161201', '70161201-Weighted-Decline-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. This exercise is excellent for abs development.', 'Crunch', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Decline Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74890da7-08d7-4869-ba3f-e5db4935e7fb', 'Half Jumping Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic jumping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, calves working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '77771201', '77771201-Half-Jumping-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Half Jumping Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Half Jumping Jack', 'burpee, high_knees, jump_rope', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('749cedb5-44e7-4494-8685-ff9b8e361669', 'Bridge Hip Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '1441201', '01441201-Bridge-Hip-Abduction_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. This exercise is excellent for glutes development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Bridge Hip Abduction', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74a09f66-ce7a-4539-9be0-1b66eaa1bf30', 'Side Bend (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '10191201', '10191201-Band-side-bend-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Side Bend. 2. Set up in the starting position for Band Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('74a43b3e-6394-43bf-8c01-85513b99f671', 'Press (Kettlebell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '5201201', '05201201-Kettlebell-Alternating-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Alternating Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Press - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('74abe836-f65d-47d1-b169-1b89f35dc31c', 'Standing Lateral Raise (Plate)', 'Shoulders', 'Weight Plate', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '64851201', '64851201-Weighted-Plate-Standing-Lateral-Raise-(male)_Shoul.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Weighted Plate Standing Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74ae2af5-4833-4b85-922c-408e88b0abd7', 'Opposite Marching Knee Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '90571201', '90571201-Opposite-Marching-Knee-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Opposite Marching Knee Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Opposite Marching Knee Tap', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74ca5b23-68ca-4bf1-b49f-b3ed22a6d257', 'Abduction Lunge (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this lunging movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '11591201', '11591201-Suspender-Abduction-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Abduction Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Suspender Abduction Lunge', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('74cdf947-6a40-45d3-a42f-9de5199d23ba', 'Cheerleader Clap Backhand Swing', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This swinging exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '63741201', '63741201-Cheerleader-Clap-Backhand-Swing-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Cheerleader Clap Backhand Swing', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74d7597f-9f88-42ac-8b68-d79267f59b3a', 'Single Leg Squat With Support - Pistol (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '58281201', '58281201-Dumbbell-Single-Leg-Squat-with-Support-(pistol)_Th.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat With Support', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('74dedf1b-3fdb-4b55-985f-e1537e6ee989', 'Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors, grip work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '4741201', '04741201-Hanging-Straight-Leg-Hip-Raise_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74e0542e-d74b-443f-b217-7a46064c45bc', 'Standing Outer Push', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '86031201', '86031201-Bodyweight-Standing-Outer-Push-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Standing Outer Push. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Outer Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74ee465a-af57-4040-8360-161561bd4f6f', 'Half Squat Side Bend', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '64741201', '64741201-Half-Squat-Side-Bend-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Include this in your core training.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Half Squat Side Bend', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('74fe8829-97f1-4df4-b663-2f1d02017c83', 'Incline Row (Kettlebell)', 'Back', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Incline Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '68241201', '68241201-Kettlebell-Incline-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Incline Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Incline Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('750318a4-52d8-4c05-bc71-5e7840c1e8f2', 'Single Leg Sliding Floor Bridge Curl (Towel)', 'Arms', 'Towel', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this curling movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '35141201', '35141201-Single-Leg-Sliding-Floor-Bridge-Curl-on-Towel_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Single Leg Sliding Floor Bridge Curl On Towel. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Sliding Floor Bridge Curl On Towel', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75038551-a4b3-4671-b103-4f20ed1a30e3', 'Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Romanian Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '22131201', '22131201-Barbell-Romanian-Deadlift-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Hip Hinge', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('7512e418-d712-4eee-b582-69c4cfd3e4db', 'Russian Twist Chop', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '59381201', '59381201-Russian-Twist-Chop-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Russian Twist Chop. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist Chop', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75137a3d-0a2d-4dc9-9712-39ae7d0170d7', 'Plank 3 Point Hops', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stabilization movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '69851201', '69851201-Plank-3-Point-Hops-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank 3 Point Hops', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7514175e-388f-4e57-a0d5-54dc040e7b85', 'Incline Fly (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Fly Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '58431201', '58431201-Lever-Incline-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Incline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lever Incline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('751e5871-8661-431a-8668-89dd7b4e32be', 'Jump Pistol Squat Box', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Jump Pistol Squat Box builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '41681201', '41681201-Jump-Pistol-Squat-Box-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 5. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Jump Pistol Squat Box', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75204eea-0a45-41f7-9194-cd4f1c996177', 'Standing Shoulder Press (Smith Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Smith Machine', '{Deltoids}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '12241201', '12241201-Smith-Standing-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Standing Shoulder Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Smith Standing Shoulder Press', 'Standing Shoulder Press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('752557e8-188e-47da-bb10-9bf3997c1fbd', 'Balance Disk Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Balance Disk Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '98071201', '98071201-Balance-Disk-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Balance Disk Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7535fdb0-7cea-4475-9c7d-3d59c7c236fd', 'Hopping Knee Drive', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Hopping Knee Drive is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '78491201', '78491201-Hopping-Knee-Drive-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hopping Knee Drive. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Hopping Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('754cbf95-23ea-4d0d-b65e-06655e821656', 'Pulse Goblet Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Pulse Goblet Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '97021201', '97021201-Bodyweight-Pulse-Goblet-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Pulse Goblet Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('754e48ba-4ba0-4508-a28c-c63a3e1ae90d', 'Inverted Row Bent Knees', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '70201201', '70201201-Inverted-Row-Bent-Knees-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Great for building strength in your upper back.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Inverted Row Bent Knees', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('755a55e9-e5c6-49c9-8bc2-feb3e7e46e1f', 'Narrow Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '65021201', '65021201-Bodyweight-Narrow-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Narrow Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('755aa08a-c8dc-4900-ae11-2b3ee27d0894', 'Side Lying Reverse Clamshell', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. The hip abductors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '93881201', '93881201-Side-Lying-Reverse-Clamshell-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Reverse Clamshell. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Side Lying Reverse Clamshell', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75669315-c2bc-4a58-bb73-b744ca68670b', 'Bent Over Y Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '79951201', '79951201-Dumbbell-Bent-over-Y-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Y Raise. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Bent Over Y Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Bent Over Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('757bc0f0-247f-4a3c-90fc-84d32014609b', 'Overhead Triceps Extension (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '9141201', '09141201-Band-overhead-triceps-extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('759671ab-9381-419f-abc1-f587153f1341', 'Standing Incline Bird Dog Crunch (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Target your erector spinae with this crunching exercise for a stronger posterior chain. Secondary activation of your glutes, abs provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '88861201', '88861201-Standing-Incline-Bird-Dog-Crunch-against-Wall-(mal.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Standing Incline Bird Dog Crunch Against Wall', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75a17dd9-9f06-413e-95b1-55ebc369d12c', 'Seated Side Bend (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '83111201', '83111201-Seated-Side-Bend-on-a-Chair-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Seated Side Bend On A Chair', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75b601b1-67c8-4dbc-86ce-ed88a1d231d5', 'Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Incline Bench Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '3141201', '03141201-Dumbbell-Incline-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Bench Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('75c7166c-5740-4986-96e6-30e028d41992', 'Horse Stance Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67141201', '67141201-Horse-Stance-Squat-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. An effective movement for your legs routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Horse Stance Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75ca9d3f-79a0-480f-9366-97f010af5618', 'Balance Board Single Leg Balance', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '107331201', '107331201-Balance-Board-Single-Leg-Balance-(male)_Stretchin.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Balance Board Single Leg Balance. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Balance Board Single Leg Balance', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75d317e0-949a-4078-b638-be5874f437e7', 'Lying Floor Leg Raise - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '81201', '00081201-Alternate-Lying-Floor-Leg-Raise_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Alternate Lying Floor Leg Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Alternate Lying Floor Leg Raise. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Floor Leg Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75d5e0e1-0f51-45dc-9bd3-205a2dd0a7a5', 'Bent Over Shoulder Pendulum', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your delts. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '64381201', '64381201-Bent-Over-Shoulder-Pendulum-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bent Over Shoulder Pendulum. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Bent Over Shoulder Pendulum', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75d895d5-7722-497b-a45f-ce99d9fb1d7a', 'Goblet Wall Sit (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this movement movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '75591201', '75591201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Wall-Sit-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Wall Sit. 2. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'wall_sit', 'Goblet Wall Sit', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('75e685d9-4eb0-4faf-80b9-a9c772c0e7fc', '90 To 90 (Leaning)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '85291201', '85291201-90-to-90-Lean-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90 Lean. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Static / Mobility', 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '90 To 90', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75eb938c-9f42-4da9-b55e-0da8dc72a795', 'Standing Trapezius Press (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Standing Trapezius Press is a compound pressing exercise that engages your entire body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '92091201', '92091201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Trapezius-Press-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Trapezius Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Resistance Band Standing Trapezius Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Trapezius Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('75f29f6a-d317-467e-91cb-c2bdc2c78079', 'Front Plank Open And Close', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '78331201', '78331201-Front-Plank-Open-and-Close-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Open And Close', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75f62635-e5c0-4a21-9920-a0424eacb6dd', 'Lying Floor Negative Dragon Flag', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Floor Negative Dragon Flag, focusing on your abs. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '93181201', '93181201-Lying-Floor-Negative-Dragon-Flag_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Floor Negative Dragon Flag. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Floor Negative Dragon Flag. 3. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Floor Negative Dragon Flag', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('75f77bba-e7be-4e71-bb99-15c8b05b3228', 'Kickback - Neutral Grip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '45661201', '45661201-Cable-Neutral-Grip-Kickback_Upper-arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Neutral Grip Kickback. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Kickback - Neutral Grip', 'Kickback - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('75fc0098-40f4-42de-b176-704a52abfd68', 'Bent Arm Lift', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '73691201', '73691201-Bent-Arm-Lift-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bent Arm Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Bent Arm Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('760c3f87-a345-42bd-afeb-fe5d28e479fe', 'Seated Row (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '79981201', '79981201-Resistance-Band-Seated-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Seated Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('7615183e-421a-41f4-a122-f915a73875c6', 'Ring Extended Plank (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '78771201', '78771201-Ring-Extended-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. This exercise is excellent for abs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Ring Extended Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('761d0139-8781-492b-b998-7e9a8768521f', 'Low Seated Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '59641201', '59641201-Cable-Low-Seated-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the lowest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Low Seated Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('7629a565-e82b-4ecd-a052-02357c96cf8f', 'Weighted Full Can Exercise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '58181201', '58181201-Weighted-Full-Can-Exercise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Full Can Exercise. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Weighted Full Can Exercise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76487ea9-44e7-4c3b-9ccb-f09caf02e4ad', 'Front Lat Pulldown - Close Grip (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Close Grip Front Lat Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '37541201', '37541201-Cable-Close-Grip-Front-Lat-Pulldown-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Close Grip Front Lat Pulldown. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Front Lat Pulldown - Close Grip', 'Front Lat Pulldown - Close Grip', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('76515e80-2afe-4ff9-848b-bb616c78a68c', 'Cambered Bar Lying Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '2481201', '02481201-Cambered-Bar-Lying-Row_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cambered Bar Lying Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Cambered Bar Lying Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('765756f6-4bda-4f7f-9aab-e49dcf931835', 'Behind Back Finger Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '16101201', '16101201-Barbell-Behind-Back-Finger-Curl_Forearms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Behind Back Finger Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Behind Back Finger Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('76592892-7c4f-44ec-ba73-ad6886ec8101', 'Above Head Chest Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your chest, the Above Head Chest Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '45141201', '45141201-Above-Head-Chest-Stretch-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Above Head Chest Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Above Head Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('766a6931-97dc-4927-803c-5733ac0e3bb0', 'Standing Switching Arm Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Switching Arm Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '96171201', '96171201-Standing-Switching-Arm-Stretch-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Switching Arm Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Switching Arm Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76a695d0-c487-4946-a18f-0b2e2106a941', 'Seated Hip Internal Rotation (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this rotation movement focusing on your rotator cuff. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '9961201', '09961201-Band-Seated-Hip-Internal-Rotation_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Seated Hip Internal Rotation. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Band Seated Hip Internal Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Seated Hip Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('76b4f2c5-57ff-4ce1-af9e-e40167c15340', 'Wrist Roller', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this movement exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '8591201', '08591201-Wrist-Roller_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wrist Roller. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Wrist Roller', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76c5546f-e0e8-4638-95b4-ef0d835d3e28', 'Weighted Chin Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Weighted Chin Up is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '107051201', '107051201-Weighted-Chin-Up-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Weighted Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76d448e1-eeb5-4bc0-b655-a075d9490262', 'Forward Wide Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '69261201', '69261201-Forward-Wide-Walk-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Forward Wide Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Forward Wide Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76d8e407-c60d-4082-af94-455586bca418', 'Step Up (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this stepping exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '10081201', '10081201-Band-Step-up_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Step Up. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 4. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 5. Step back down with control and repeat. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('76dd21c9-130e-42e7-8031-6131a3303fb2', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Low Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing Straight Arm Chest Low Fly is a flying exercise that targets your chest muscles. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '83531201', '83531201-Bodyweight-Standing-Straight-Arm-Chest-Low-Fly-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76e8a66a-7581-4dff-a5de-f07eb7524397', 'High Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '97231201', '97231201-Cable-High-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'High Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('76ea188d-9e78-4e40-bd43-a65b1212dfb8', 'Arms Circle Marching On Spot', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '71911201', '71911201-Arms-Circle-Marching-On-Spot-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arms Circle Marching On Spot. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, 'Dynamic', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, 'Standing', NULL, 'Neutral', 'Standard', 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Arms Circle Marching On Spot', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('76ee5061-d6ae-43ff-8e5f-2c9a103e6fdf', 'Lying Bench Single Leg Curl (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Secondary activation of your calves provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '98821201', '98821201-Cable-Lying-Bench-Single-Leg-Curl-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Bench Single Leg Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Bench Single Leg Curl. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lying Bench Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('76f5d6b8-a611-4a04-a6b8-2582ac5b4d20', 'Single Downward Dog', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Single Downward Dog helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hamstrings, calves, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61641201', '61641201-Single-Downward-Dog-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Single Downward Dog. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Single Downward Dog', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('770154a4-c124-4447-a2f5-b6c2d7f8d8b1', 'Prone Rear Delt Swing (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Prone Rear Delt Swing is a swinging exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '56061201', '56061201-Dumbbell-Prone-Rear-Delt-Swing_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Rear Delt Swing. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Rear Delt Swing. 3. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 4. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 5. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Prone Rear Delt Swing', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('7702439a-12b7-46b2-aa7a-0c98d855a07e', 'Standing Calf Stretch (Wall Supported)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your calves, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The standing position engages your core for stability. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '94651201', '94651201-Standing-Calf-Stretch-with-Wall-Supported-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Move into the stretch position for Standing Calf Stretch With Wall Supported. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 34, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_stretch', 'Standing Calf Stretch With Wall Supported', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('770981ac-9dc4-4a35-8951-338b4a6e8ffc', 'Decline Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '2791201', '02791201-Decline-Push-Up_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Push Up', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Decline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('770e8628-fd99-45ed-9d49-c4229784adcd', 'Overhead Hit (Resistance Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '105531201', '105531201-Resistance-Band-Overhead-Hit-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Overhead Hit. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Overhead Hit. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Overhead Hit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('770f1f3c-9b20-4115-af8e-144631da7a7b', 'Prone Incline Curl (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68281201', '68281201-Kettlebell-Prone-Incline-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Prone Incline Curl. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Kettlebell Prone Incline Curl. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 91, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_curl', 'Prone Incline Curl', 'bicep_curl, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('77209562-c906-46d7-a665-0c9b272396b1', 'Star Jump', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '7971201', '07971201-Star-Jump-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Star Jump. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Star Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('772144da-a9e6-46e8-9583-b5277f1750eb', 'Standing Shoulders Full Flexion', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This flexion exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '55071201', '55071201-Standing-Shoulders-Full-Flexion-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Shoulders Full Flexion. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Shoulders Full Flexion', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7734bbd6-b962-43aa-b9f2-4d8ae48ded70', 'Pull Up On Dip Cage - Wide Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar, Dip Bars', '{"Lats","Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '18661201', '18661201-Wide-Grip-Pull-Up-On-Dip-Cage_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Pull Up On Dip Cage - Wide Grip', 'Pull Up On Dip Cage - Wide Grip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('773c67d1-8ff9-42c2-8bac-f1c46f8bee6c', 'Lying Around The World', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '49431201', '49431201-Lying-Around-the-World-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Around The World. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Around The World. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Lying Around The World', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('775d642b-f000-4aec-b4cd-554da6c5658c', 'Standing Triple Straight Arm Chest Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '96221201', '96221201-Standing-Triple-Straight-Arm-Chest-Fly-(female)_Ch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Triple Straight Arm Chest Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('775f1c3f-9972-49e4-bafa-8afbb08cea6d', 'Side Knee Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This dynamic raising movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '65761201', '65761201-Side-Knee-Leg-Raise-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. This exercise is excellent for abs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Side Knee Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('77621244-8458-459c-a598-89f682f3b3ff', 'Lying Single Leg Hip Flexion (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Cable Lying Single Leg Hip Flexion is a lower body flexion exercise that targets your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '88751201', '88751201-Cable-Lying-Single-Leg-Hip-Flexion-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Single Leg Hip Flexion. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Single Leg Hip Flexion. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Single Leg Hip Flexion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('7774accb-fb87-48b0-a804-30d9cbc8e570', 'V Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The V Leg Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '90281201', '90281201-V-Leg-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'V Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('777a10fe-8908-4883-afac-76bbdab32851', 'Side To Side Box Shuffle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side To Side Box Shuffle builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '15881201', '15881201-Side-to-Side-Box-Shuffle_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side To Side Box Shuffle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Side To Side Box Shuffle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('777a38f1-bd97-47b4-ad1b-87c21b7b7e9d', 'Stepback Air Bike (Air Bike)', 'Full Body', 'Air Bike', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '89071201', '89071201-Stepback-Air-Bike-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stepback Air Bike. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 35, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Stepback Air Bike', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('777cb274-ab70-47d3-8a44-5b5b72977e5a', 'Isometric Hip Flexion And Glute Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your glutes, the Isometric Hip Flexion And Glute Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '81441201', '81441201-Isometric-Hip-Flexion-and-Glute-Stretch-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Isometric Hip Flexion And Glute Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 35, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_stretch', 'Isometric Hip Flexion And Glute Stretch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('77923db1-37e6-43b5-b340-5bf1696c4af4', 'Super Rom Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '106441201', '106441201-Dumbbell-Super-Rom-Lateral-Raise-(male)_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Super Rom Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Super Rom Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('77a51139-9fdc-480b-8aad-8b51ca537db5', 'Seated Crunch - Chest Pad (Machine)', 'Core', 'Ab Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '37531201', '37531201-Lever-Seated-Crunch-(chest-pad)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Crunch. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lever Seated Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('77abc4fb-4601-4fc9-8caf-a1cdfbd4475e', 'Calf Raise (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{Calves}'::text[], '{Soleus}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57301201', '57301201-Smith-Calf-Raise-(version-2)-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Calf Raise. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Smith Calf Raise', 'Calf Raise', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('77cc6a5b-86b4-4815-912e-6c68e318031a', 'Side Plank (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Side Plank is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '58791201', '58791201-Kettlebell-Side-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Side Plank. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'kettlebell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('77cf9385-5010-413f-8044-51d52be4071c', 'Low Bar Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '57191201', '57191201-Barbell-Low-Bar-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Low Bar Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Low Bar Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('77cff82e-c904-4210-b5f9-10df1becb83c', 'Seated Incline Press Calf Raise (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Seated Incline Press Calf Raise On A Chair, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your front delts, triceps working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '69031201', '69031201-Sitting-Incline-Press-Calf-Raise-on-a-Chair-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 68, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Seated Incline Press Calf Raise On A Chair', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('77da6b0f-ad8e-442e-87d3-fda4dc46649e', 'Garland Pose Malasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Garland Pose Malasana is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '9511201', '09511201-Garland-Pose-Malasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Garland Pose Malasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Garland Pose Malasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('77e3bf24-455a-4090-afb7-c6e29874356a', 'Standing Front Heel Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93721201', '93721201-Standing-Front-Heel-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Front Heel Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Front Heel Tap', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('77f89379-6d16-455a-8846-30fe176bf0a1', 'Kneeling Crunch (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Kneeling Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '1751201', '01751201-Cable-Kneeling-Crunch_Waist-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Kneeling Crunch. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Kneeling Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('780e41e9-8aaa-4156-8482-b6d832adf1d5', 'Seated Calf Raise (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Calf Raise (plate Loaded) isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '5941201', '05941201-Lever-Seated-Calf-Raise-(plate-loaded).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Calf Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Seated Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, standing_calf_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('7816045a-802c-4ebf-bfbd-2ef10fb06d21', 'Concentration Curl Arms', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '23531201', '23531201-Concentration-Curl---Arms-(WRONG-RIGHT)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Concentration Curl Arms', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7826bf36-0f03-4e6a-9644-7dee88200144', 'Lateral Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '30541201', '30541201-Cable-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('78394634-8c6c-4a52-9024-c619af122220', 'Standing Side Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Standing Side Crunch, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '58481201', '58481201-Standing-Side-Crunch-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Standing Side Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7843503c-fd8b-47cb-95b1-4c5423ccd7ed', 'Invisible Chair Pose (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '66561201', '66561201-Invisible-Chair-Pose-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Move into the stretch position for Invisible Chair Pose. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 35, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Invisible Chair Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7851f578-5d05-4485-bc4c-502e9d66c061', 'Triceps Pushdown - V Bar (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pushing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '22491201', '22491201-Cable-Triceps-Pushdown-(V-bar)-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Triceps Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Triceps Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Triceps Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('785e1ef8-22b5-4a54-9f2e-0e6323836736', 'Dynamic Bird Dog', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Dynamic Bird Dog, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your glutes, abs working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '89741201', '89741201-Dynamic-Bird-Dog-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Dynamic Bird Dog. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Dynamic Bird Dog', 'dead_bug, plank, back_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('7861f294-aa75-419f-98f2-aa4e2235ae87', 'Glute Bridge Single Leg On Bench', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Glute Bridge One Leg On Bench is a hip-dominant bridging exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '24731201', '24731201-Glute-Bridge-One-Leg-on-Bench-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge Single Leg On Bench', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('78740577-7c26-41c0-9d8a-0d6fc8613bf5', 'Prayer Push', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Prayer Push, an effective shoulder pushing exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '48761201', '48761201-Prayer-Push-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Prayer Push. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Prayer Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('787480da-5194-4a0c-aedc-672161464c11', 'Lying Leg Stretched Tap Toe To Knee Opening Knee T', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Leg Stretched Tap Toe To Knee Opening Knee T is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '84941201', '84941201-Lying-Leg-Stretched-Tap-Toe-to-Knee-Opening-Knee-t.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Stretched Tap Toe To Knee Opening Knee T. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Leg Stretched Tap Toe To Knee Opening Knee T. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying Leg Stretched Tap Toe To Knee Opening Knee T', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('787e4661-120f-49b0-988e-c536b16ff366', 'Kneeling Side Leg Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65711201', '65711201-Kneeling-Side-Leg-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Side Leg Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Side Leg Circle', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
